---
title: 'Don’t stop at the tiles'
slug: 'dont-stop-at-the-tiles'
date: '2026-09-04'
excerpt: 'Tiles can feel like winning. Prove is where it sticks.'
tags: ['doctrinal-mastery', 'student-tip']
author: 'Patrick'
---

Scripture Builder tiles can feel like winning. You puzzle the phrases and they click into place. The verse looks right, and it is tempting to leave it at that.

You have done real work putting the verse together. Now it is time to **Prove** — that is where it can stick.

Go up one level to the verse with first-letter hints. Get that down a few times. Then type it cold — no prompts, no tiles. That is the moment you know you know it.

Stick with the same verse until you can produce the words without the board. This takes you one step closer to mastery, and it lets the doctrine come back when you need it.
